# Vocabulary lookup uses only free, offline-friendly sources (bundled WordNet + the community
# Free Dictionary API + CC-CEDICT) and needs NO API keys. This file documents the optional
# server settings; copy it to .env only if you want to override a default.

# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=3000
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# DATABASE_DIR=
# The `dev` script persists to a git-ignored .data/db by default; `start` is in-memory. Set
# DATABASE_DIR to a path to choose your own location, or "" to force in-memory under `dev`.
# SOURCE_FILES_DIR=./.data/sources
# IMAGE_RESOURCES_DIR=./.data/images
# Durable file roots kept for provenance: SOURCE_FILES_DIR holds uploaded source files, and
# IMAGE_RESOURCES_DIR holds extracted image resources. `pnpm data:backup` captures the database plus
# both of these roots into one verified archive; `pnpm data:restore` loads them into a fresh, empty
# target. See docs/BACKUP.md. Keep archives out of git.
# EPUB_UPLOAD_LIMIT_BYTES=52428800
# WEB_DIR=
# Single-origin deploy (see docs/DEPLOY.md): set WEB_DIR to the built web client
# (src/apps/web/dist) and the server also serves the app at `/` alongside `/api/*`. Unset in dev,
# where Vite serves the client separately.

# COACH_API_KEY=
# Cloud key for the coach's strong tier (the end-of-round judge). Unset = coach runs entirely on the
# local Ollama models (or the deterministic fake until they are pulled). Never commit a real key.
# COACH_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# EXPLAIN_MODEL=qwen2.5
# COACH_CONVERSE_TIER=cheap
# COACH_ANALYZE_TIER=cheap
# The local coach + lookup "AI 解释" aid. The easiest way to fill these in is `pnpm setup:coach`,
# which installs Ollama (with a Y/N prompt), pulls the converse model (COACH_MODEL, default
# llama3.1:8b) + the 文言 explain model (EXPLAIN_MODEL, default qwen2.5), and writes COACH_MODEL +
# EXPLAIN_MODEL + both tiers=cheap here for a fully-local coach (so the server serves the exact models
# it pulled). For the optional cloud judge instead, set COACH_API_KEY and COACH_ANALYZE_TIER=strong.
# Per-call tier overrides (cheap = local Ollama, strong = cloud): also COACH_AUTHOR_TIER /
# COACH_PROPOSE_TIER / COACH_JUDGE_TIER. See docs/COACH.md.

# WHISPER_BINARY=
# WHISPER_MODEL_PATH=
# WHISPER_LANGUAGE=
# Local Whisper STT for spoken practice (see docs/SPEECH.md). Both WHISPER_BINARY (the whisper CLI /
# wrapper launcher) and WHISPER_MODEL_PATH (a faster-whisper model size like `small`/`base.en`, or a
# path) must be set to enable it; WHISPER_LANGUAGE (default `en`) is optional. Unset = spoken practice
# transcribes to empty. The easiest way to fill these in is `pnpm setup:voice`, which installs the
# wrapper, fetches the model, and writes these three values here.
